{"study_accession":"PRJDB18160","secondary_study_accession":"DRP013476","title":"RNA sequencing and analysis of human eosinophils stimulated with NOD2 ligand and IL-5","description":"Activated eosinophils are a major cell type involved in allergic diseases. IL-5 primarily activates eosinophils and prolongs their survival. However, interactions between these cells and microorganisms are also important for further activation. NOD2 (Nucleotide-binding oligomerization domain-containing protein 2) is an intracellular pattern recognition receptor that plays a key role in the immune system. It recognizes muramyl dipeptide (MDP), a component of bacterial cell walls. The aim of this study is to clarify the role of NOD2 as a key receptor for human eosinophil activation.","pubmed":"39307590","geo_series":"","n_samples":16,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMD00787874","study_accession":"PRJDB18160","blood_class":"blood_cells","class_from":"sample","title":"DK22231_01","description":"HP1 Human eosinophils, non-stimulated","sex":"not collected","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2025-06-23","attributes":[["collection_date","2023-08-01"],["health_state","healthy"],["INSDC secondary accession","DRS483488"],["aliquot","1"],["ethnicity","Japanese"],["organism","Homo sapiens"],["race","Asian"],["sex","not collected"],["tissue","blood"],["sample_type","primary cell"],["isolate","Keio University"],["NCBI submission package","Human.1.0"],["geo_loc_name","Japan:Tokyo, Shinjuku-ku, Shinanomachi"],["cell_subtype","white blood cell"],["cell_type","eosinophil"],["age","not collected"],["biomaterial_provider","Keio University"],["sample_name","L-Medium-1"],["BioSampleModel","Human"],["ENA-FIRST-PUBLIC","2025-06-19"],["ENA-LAST-UPDATE","2025-06-19"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"DRR568508","experiment_accession":"DRX551975","library_layout":"SINGLE","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"NextSeq 500","read_count":2194637,"base_count":166792412,"first_publ